assistant_response:
```java
class Vehicle {
    protected String color;
    public Vehicle(String color) { this.color = color; }
}
class Car extends Vehicle {
    private String fuelType;
    public Car(String color, String fuelType) {
        super(color);
        this.fuelType = fuelType;
    }
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Color: " + color);
        System.out.println("Fuel Type: " + fuelType);
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Car("Red", "Diesel").display();
    }
}
```
This is a complete compilable repair, initializing the inherited color through Vehicle's one-argument constructor.
